**Materials:**

* Arduino Uno
* 4 wheels
* Ultrasonic sensor (HC-SR04)
* 3 LED bulbs
* 3 Buzzers
* Jumper wires
* 9V battery

**Circuit:**

* Connect the ultrasonic sensor to the Arduino Uno as follows:
    * VCC to 5V
    * Trig to digital pin 9
    * Echo to digital pin 10
    * GND to GND
* Connect each LED and buzzer to the Arduino Uno as follows:
    * LED+ to digital pin 2
    * LED- to GND
    * Buzzer+ to digital pin 4
    * Buzzer- to GND
* Connect the 9V battery to the Arduino Uno.

**Code:**

```c++
// Define the LED and buzzer pins
const int ledPin = 2;
const int buzzerPin = 4;

// Define the ultrasonic sensor pins
const int trigPin = 9;
const int echoPin = 10;

// Define the distance threshold for train detection
const int distanceThreshold = 20; // Adjust this value based on the desired detection distance

void setup() {
  // Set up the LED and buzzer pins as outputs
  pinMode(ledPin, OUTPUT);
  pinMode(buzzerPin, OUTPUT);

  // Set up the ultrasonic sensor pins
  pinMode(trigPin, OUTPUT);
  pinMode(echoPin, INPUT);
}

void loop() {
  // Trigger the ultrasonic sensor by sending a pulse of 10 microseconds
  digitalWrite(trigPin, HIGH);
  delayMicroseconds(10);
  digitalWrite(trigPin, LOW);

  // Read the echo signal from the sensor and calculate the distance
  long duration = pulseIn(echoPin, HIGH);
  float distance = duration * 0.034 / 2; // Convert duration to centimeters

  // Check if the train is too close
  if (distance < distanceThreshold) {
    // Turn on the LED and buzzer to indicate train presence
    digitalWrite(ledPin, HIGH);
    digitalWrite(buzzerPin, HIGH);
  } else {
    // Turn off the LED and buzzer to indicate no train presence
    digitalWrite(ledPin, LOW);
    digitalWrite(buzzerPin, LOW);
  }
}
```

**Setup:**

* Assemble the 4 wheels to the base of the Arduino Uno.
* Mount the ultrasonic sensor on a pole and connect it to the appropriate pins on the Arduino Uno.
* Set up the 3 poles with the LEDs and buzzers and connect them to the appropriate pins on the Arduino Uno.
* Connect the 9V battery to the Arduino Uno.
* Upload the code to the Arduino Uno.

**Usage:**

* Place the train accident prevention system near the tracks.
* When a train approaches within the detection distance threshold, the LED will turn on and the buzzer will sound, alerting you to the train's presence.
